millions of young faithful thronged  copacabana beach for an  open-air mass that resembled a gigantic  party the crowds grew  every day during pope francis's visit to  brazil for world youth day  this was the final chance to see the  pontiff before his return to the vatican  in his homily francis called on young  catholics to spread the message of the  gospel around the world  the pope said it was good to be here for  world youth day  and to share our faith together with  young people  now it's your turn to pass this  experience on to others  jesus calls on you to be disciples on a  mission  brazilian president dima rousseff and  other south american heads of state  attended the mass  silence for more than a minute after the  sermon as the crowd reflected on what  they'd heard  the pope's mission was to spark new  interest in catholicism  among young people and present a more  down-to-earth church  judging by the interests he seems to  have succeeded  a message francis plans to maintain  through the next world youth day  slated for poland in 2016.
 

